1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,860
这是其中一期视频早期草稿里的一帧暂停画面
Here's what a paused frame looked like in an early draft of one of these videos,

2
00:00:04,860 --> 00:00:07,168
那期讲井字棋，给 12 岁左右的孩子看
about tic-tac-toe, for kids around 12.

3
00:00:07,488 --> 00:00:11,733
看右边这一行：4 乘 3 乘 2，然后是 12
Look at the line on the right: 4 times 3 times 2, and then 12.

4
00:00:11,967 --> 00:00:13,389
先暂停一下
Pause for a moment.

5
00:00:13,439 --> 00:00:15,999
如果你 12 岁，你会觉得这里哪儿出错了？
If you were 12, what would you think went wrong here?

6
00:00:22,233 --> 00:00:25,604
看起来像是乘法算错了，但数学其实没错
It looks like bad multiplication, but the math was right.

7
00:00:25,924 --> 00:00:30,702
这个 12 是一个正往 24 涨的计数，却摆在了算式那一行上
The 12 was a running count on its way to 24, sitting on the formula's line.

8
00:00:31,022 --> 00:00:32,466
是排版在撒谎
The layout lied.

9
00:00:32,516 --> 00:00:34,628
而发现问题的评审，并不是孩子
And the reviewer who caught it wasn't a child.

10
00:00:34,948 --> 00:00:37,785
它是一个 AI，假扮成 12 岁的孩子
It was an AI, pretending to be a 12-year-old.

11
00:00:38,033 --> 00:00:39,633
奇怪的地方来了
Now the strange part.

12
00:00:39,825 --> 00:00:43,572
这些视频里几乎所有东西都是 AI 智能体做的
Almost everything in these videos was made by AI agents:

13
00:00:43,572 --> 00:00:46,716
脚本、动画代码，还有各种检查
the script, the animation code, and the checks.

14
00:00:47,036 --> 00:00:49,958
可它们没有一个能听见旁白，也没法按下播放键
And none of them can hear the narration, or press play.

15
00:00:50,278 --> 00:00:52,113
那它们怎么知道这些行不行？
So how do they know any of it works?

16
00:00:52,350 --> 00:00:57,905
这期视频会讲：整条流水线，谁做了什么，没有眼睛和耳朵怎么检查
This video covers the pipeline, who did what, how work gets checked without eyes or ears,

17
00:00:57,905 --> 00:01:02,462
中文版，哪些事仍然需要人，以及下一步改进什么
the Chinese versions, what still needs a human, and what to improve next.

18
00:01:04,100 --> 00:01:06,440
一切从一个人开始，也就是这位用户
It started with one person, the user:

19
00:01:06,440 --> 00:01:09,476
一位论文多到读不过来的研究者
a researcher with more papers to read than time.

20
00:01:09,796 --> 00:01:11,977
视频的风格学的是 3Blue1Brown
The look comes from 3Blue1Brown,

21
00:01:11,977 --> 00:01:16,815
这个频道的视频用 Manim 做动画，每一帧都是用代码画出来的
whose videos are animated in Manim, where every frame is drawn by code.

22
00:01:17,135 --> 00:01:21,245
本项目的想法来自 Andrej Karpathy 的帖子
The idea for this project came from a post by Andrej Karpathy,

23
00:01:21,245 --> 00:01:23,300
是第一个请求里引用的
as quoted in the first request.

24
00:01:23,533 --> 00:01:25,483
用户自己的话说得更进一步
The user's own words go further:

25
00:01:25,483 --> 00:01:29,016
我们的大脑就是一个神经网络，训练它是要吃苦的
our brain is a neural net, and training it takes hardship.

26
00:01:29,336 --> 00:01:34,228
用户说，AI 很有耐心，可自己却在做大量的“认知卸载”
AI is patient, they said, but they were doing a lot of cognitive offloading:

27
00:01:34,228 --> 00:01:36,803
让 AI 替自己思考
letting the AI do the thinking for them.

28
00:01:37,050 --> 00:01:40,229
视频应该像一位导师，讲清楚论文之间怎样关联
A video should be a mentor, showing how papers connect,

29
00:01:40,229 --> 00:01:42,021
因为论文从来不是孤立的
because they're never isolated.

30
00:01:42,341 --> 00:01:46,319
而视频只是第一步：下一步是能交互的东西
And video is only a first step: the next is something interactive,

31
00:01:46,319 --> 00:01:48,549
学习的人得亲手做出点什么
where the learner has to make things.

32
00:01:48,783 --> 00:01:50,383
接下来是四个请求
Then came four requests.

33
00:01:50,639 --> 00:01:55,439
一篇朋友发来的、讲隐私的论文，用户自己没读过，这样测试才公平
A privacy paper from a friend, which the user hadn't read, to keep the test fair.

34
00:01:55,759 --> 00:01:58,468
一期井字棋视频，给一个初中生看
A tic-tac-toe video, for a middle-school kid.

35
00:01:58,788 --> 00:02:00,388
这两期的中文版
Chinese versions of both.

36
00:02:00,666 --> 00:02:02,266
还有这期视频
And this video.

37
00:02:03,983 --> 00:02:05,946
团队：一个真人，就是用户
The team: one human, the user.

38
00:02:06,266 --> 00:02:08,484
一个 AI 智能体：Claude Code
One AI agent: Claude Code.

39
00:02:08,804 --> 00:02:10,877
它手下有 183 个子智能体
Under it, 183 sub-agents

40
00:02:10,877 --> 00:02:14,244
来自 46 次工作流运行，都在这期视频之前
in 46 workflow runs, before this video.

41
00:02:14,564 --> 00:02:17,886
工作流就是智能体为了启动子智能体写的程序
A workflow is a script the agent writes to launch sub-agents,

42
00:02:17,886 --> 00:02:19,486
每个子智能体只干一件事
each with one job.

43
00:02:19,706 --> 00:02:22,941
还有各种工具，比如每种语言各一个合成语音
And tools, like a synthetic voice for each language

44
00:02:22,941 --> 00:02:24,541
以及一个语音识别模型
and a speech recognizer.

45
00:02:24,700 --> 00:02:27,729
值得学什么、讲给谁听，是用户定的
The user decided what was worth learning, and for whom.

46
00:02:28,049 --> 00:02:33,844
用户上传了 36 个 PDF，给出了井字棋视频要讲的那些数
They uploaded 36 PDFs, gave the tic-tac-toe counts to explain,

47
00:02:33,844 --> 00:02:39,825
比如 255,168 种对局，还提供了那期视频讲解的程序
like 255,168 games, and supplied the program that video teaches.

48
00:02:40,145 --> 00:02:41,589
程序本来就能用
It already worked.

49
00:02:41,639 --> 00:02:46,097
智能体只是把一个数字 0 改成了字母 O，又重写了注释
The agent only changed a zero into the letter O, and rewrote the comments.

50
00:02:46,333 --> 00:02:47,933
剩下的都是智能体做的
The agent did the rest.

51
00:02:48,125 --> 00:02:50,707
它写了驱动整条流水线的工具包
It wrote the toolkit that runs the pipeline,

52
00:02:50,707 --> 00:02:53,464
一百多个 commit 里，除了两个，全是它提交的
and made all but two of over a hundred commits,

53
00:02:53,464 --> 00:02:55,165
commit 就是项目存下的版本
the project's saved versions.

54
00:02:55,485 --> 00:02:59,112
不到一周，工作因为用量上限至少停了六次
In under a week, work stopped at least six times on usage limits.

55
00:02:59,432 --> 00:03:04,594
其中有两次，额度恢复之后它又闲了好几个小时，直到用户催了一下
Twice, it then sat idle for hours after the limit reset, until the user nudged it.

56
00:03:05,583 --> 00:03:09,894
从请求到成片，差分隐私那期用了大约六个小时
From request to final cut, the privacy video took about six hours,

57
00:03:09,894 --> 00:03:11,983
井字棋那期三个多小时
and tic-tac-toe just over three.

58
00:03:12,303 --> 00:03:16,868
中文版花的时间长得多：分别是 16 个小时和大约两天
The Chinese versions took far longer: 16 hours, and about two days.

59
00:03:17,188 --> 00:03:20,047
最终画面的渲染，每期都不到半小时
Drawing the final frames took under half an hour each.

60
00:03:20,367 --> 00:03:24,050
其余的时间都花在：翻译，一轮又一轮的评审和修改
The rest went to translating, rounds of review and fixes,

61
00:03:24,050 --> 00:03:27,215
返工了四次的字幕工具，还有等待
a subtitle tool reworked four times, and waiting.

62
00:03:27,535 --> 00:03:32,218
屏幕上的费用，是整个会话截至 10 月 7 日的花费
And the cost on screen is what the whole session had cost by October 7th,

63
00:03:32,218 --> 00:03:36,452
按公开的按量计费价格计算：涵盖全部四个请求，不是一期视频
at the public pay-per-use price: all four requests, not one video.

64
00:03:38,100 --> 00:03:40,395
这条流水线是一串文件
The pipeline is a chain of files:

65
00:03:40,395 --> 00:03:46,932
论文、目录记录、带页码的论文笔记，再到脚本、动画代码和视频
a paper, a catalog entry, a digest with page numbers, a script, animation code, and the video.

66
00:03:47,252 --> 00:03:51,476
每一步都留下一个文件，所以随时可以停下、检查，再接着做
Every step leaves a file behind, so you can stop, review, and resume.

67
00:03:51,850 --> 00:03:53,450
每个文件都要检查
Each file gets checked.

68
00:03:53,621 --> 00:03:57,921
给论文编目录的智能体不光看文件名，还读了内容
Agents cataloging the papers read them, not just their names,

69
00:03:57,921 --> 00:04:01,727
结果发现 36 个 PDF 里有 4 个是错的论文
and found that 4 of the 36 PDFs were the wrong papers.

70
00:04:02,047 --> 00:04:05,653
差分隐私论文的笔记里，甚至列出了论文本身的错误
And the privacy digest even lists the paper's own mistakes.

71
00:04:07,050 --> 00:04:11,496
在脚本里，每一小段都是一行画面配一行台词
In the script, each beat pairs a show line, the picture, with a say line:

72
00:04:11,496 --> 00:04:13,749
台词就是语音要一字不差念出来的话
the exact words the voice will speak.

73
00:04:14,069 --> 00:04:17,503
动画代码直接从这个文件里读取这些台词
The animation code reads those words straight from this file.

74
00:04:17,823 --> 00:04:21,557
脚本是写给耳朵听的：“九的阶乘”要用文字写出来
It's written for the ear: nine factorial is spelled out in words.

75
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:25,302
所以在做任何动画之前，先让别的智能体评审脚本
So other agents review the script before any animation:

76
00:04:25,302 --> 00:04:30,141
改一句话只要几秒钟，场景做完了再改，就得整个重画
a sentence takes seconds to fix, but a finished scene has to be drawn again.

77
00:04:30,461 --> 00:04:33,640
第一天，智能体就把这条规则写进了自己的工作指南
The agent wrote that rule into its own guide on day one.

78
00:04:33,960 --> 00:04:38,952
几分钟后，评审还在进行，它就启动了六个子智能体去做场景
Minutes later, it started six sub-agents building scenes while the review was still running.

79
00:04:39,272 --> 00:04:43,639
11 分钟后，一份要求改脚本的评审意见回来了
Eleven minutes after that, one review came back with changes to the script,

80
00:04:43,639 --> 00:04:45,239
于是六个全被叫停
so all six were stopped.

81
00:04:45,459 --> 00:04:50,387
光把规则写下来还不够：工作流本身就得等评审结束
Writing the rule down was not enough: the workflow itself has to wait for the review.

82
00:04:51,733 --> 00:04:53,326
接下来是动画
Now the animation.

83
00:04:53,376 --> 00:04:58,880
在这条流水线里，先生成语音，动画等的是词，不是秒数
In this pipeline, the voice is made first, and the animation waits for words, not seconds.

84
00:04:59,200 --> 00:05:03,210
这段代码的意思是：旁白念到“A hundred”，就显示一百
This code says: when the narration reaches "A hundred", show a hundred.

85
00:05:03,530 --> 00:05:05,813
念到“A million”，就显示一百万
When it reaches "A million", show a million.

86
00:05:06,050 --> 00:05:10,914
语音是一句一句合成的，所以每一句从哪儿开始，都精确知道
The voice speaks one sentence at a time, so every sentence start is known exactly.

87
00:05:11,234 --> 00:05:13,794
可在一句话内部，工具包只能靠猜
Inside a sentence, the toolkit has to guess.

88
00:05:14,114 --> 00:05:17,335
它假设每个字符念起来都花一样的时间
It assumes every character takes the same time to say.

89
00:05:17,583 --> 00:05:19,005
暂停一下，自己试试
Pause and try it.

90
00:05:19,055 --> 00:05:23,258
屏幕上这个数有 7 个字符，和英文单词 example 一样多
The number on screen has 7 characters, as many as the word example.

91
00:05:23,578 --> 00:05:25,178
把两个都大声念出来
Say both out loud.

92
00:05:25,242 --> 00:05:26,842
念这个数要多久？
How long does the number take?

93
00:05:35,083 --> 00:05:39,520
大约三秒：三十六万两千八百八十
About three seconds: three hundred sixty-two thousand, eight hundred eighty.

94
00:05:39,840 --> 00:05:41,440
比那个单词长得多
Far longer than the word.

95
00:05:41,654 --> 00:05:46,006
所以对紧跟在它后面的那些词，工具包的估计早了将近两秒
So the toolkit's guess for the words right after it lands almost two seconds early.

96
00:05:46,250 --> 00:05:48,079
目前的办法是手动修
The fix so far is manual:

97
00:05:48,079 --> 00:05:53,418
光这一个场景就有大约 20 处手动设的偏移，最大的一处是 2.2 秒
this one scene carries about 20 hand-set shifts, the biggest 2.2 seconds.

98
00:05:53,738 --> 00:05:55,698
更好的办法其实触手可及
A better fix is within reach:

99
00:05:55,698 --> 00:06:00,159
中文用的那个在线语音服务，能把每个词的时间一起发回来
the online voice used for Chinese can send the time of every word.

100
00:06:00,479 --> 00:06:04,276
但工具包现在还没去要这些时间，只保存了音频
But the toolkit doesn't ask for them yet, and keeps only the audio.

101
00:06:06,917 --> 00:06:08,211
暂停想一想
Pause and think.

102
00:06:08,261 --> 00:06:10,842
假设你听不见，也没法按播放键
Suppose you can't hear, and you can't press play.

103
00:06:11,162 --> 00:06:12,762
你会怎么检查一个视频？
How would you check a video?

104
00:06:20,900 --> 00:06:24,975
智能体的答案是：把时间变成图片，把声音变成文字
The agent's answer: turn time into pictures, and sound into text.

105
00:06:25,295 --> 00:06:30,543
工具包先快速渲染一版草稿，每两秒取一张截图，拼成一张网格图
The toolkit renders a quick draft, and tiles a still from every two seconds into one grid.

106
00:06:30,863 --> 00:06:34,276
智能体能看图片，所以它就是这样“看”视频的
An agent can look at an image, so this is how it watches.

107
00:06:34,517 --> 00:06:36,813
两张截图之间也可能出问题
Between stills, things can go wrong,

108
00:06:36,813 --> 00:06:40,768
所以为了检查动作，它会每隔五分之一秒抓一帧
so to check motion, it grabs frames a fifth of a second apart.

109
00:06:41,088 --> 00:06:43,242
如果几帧都一样，就是什么都没动
If they're all the same, nothing moved.

110
00:06:43,484 --> 00:06:45,425
然后，凡是能测量的，它都测量
Then it measures everything it can.

111
00:06:45,745 --> 00:06:49,783
有个叫 lint 的检查工具，一帧都不画就能把每个场景跑一遍
A checker called a lint runs each scene without drawing a frame,

112
00:06:49,783 --> 00:06:54,641
标出跑到屏幕外的东西、太小的文字，还有最后没清掉的元素
and flags anything off screen, text that's too small, or objects left behind.

113
00:06:54,961 --> 00:06:57,508
井字棋那期的场景还会自己检查自己
And the tic-tac-toe scenes check themselves,

114
00:06:57,508 --> 00:07:00,230
针对画面上的数字和棋盘，一共有 82 项检查
with 82 checks on the numbers and boards shown.

115
00:07:02,250 --> 00:07:05,962
接下来是评审：一批全新的智能体，没有参与制作这个视频
Next come the reviewers, fresh agents that didn't build the video.

116
00:07:06,282 --> 00:07:11,164
它们拿到的是截图、代替声音的字幕和一个角色
They get the stills, the subtitles as a stand-in for sound, and a role:

117
00:07:11,164 --> 00:07:15,221
导演，或者一个模拟的 12 岁孩子，聪明但普通
a director, or a simulated 12-year-old, sharp but ordinary.

118
00:07:15,541 --> 00:07:20,341
这个模拟的孩子找出了真问题，比如有些表示走法的标签，它读不懂
That simulated kid found real problems, like move labels it couldn't decode.

119
00:07:20,583 --> 00:07:25,020
第一轮找出了 30 个问题，其中就有算式那一行上的那个 12
Round one found 30 issues, including that 12 on the formula line.

120
00:07:25,340 --> 00:07:29,006
第二轮，一位新的导演逐条复查
In round two, a fresh director re-checked each one:

121
00:07:29,006 --> 00:07:31,378
25 个已经修好，5 个只修好了一部分
25 were fixed, and 5 only partly.

122
00:07:34,017 --> 00:07:35,809
导演还抓到一个更隐蔽的 bug
The director caught a subtler bug.

123
00:07:36,129 --> 00:07:39,284
这个场景本该把 4 个棋子换遍全部 24 种顺序
The scene should shuffle 4 marks through all 24 orders,

124
00:07:39,284 --> 00:07:42,038
可棋盘一动不动，计数器却还在往上跳
but the board froze while the counter ticked on.

125
00:07:42,358 --> 00:07:44,181
原因是 Manim 的一个坑
The cause is a Manim pitfall:

126
00:07:44,181 --> 00:07:49,712
所有移动都在第一步播放之前就设好了，而每次设置都会覆盖前一次
every move was set up before the first one played, and each setup erased the one before,

127
00:07:49,712 --> 00:07:52,918
结果每个棋子直接跳到最后的位置，然后就不动了
so each mark jumped to its last spot and sat still.

128
00:07:53,238 --> 00:07:57,206
现在每一步移动都等到播放时才设置，棋子就又动起来了
Now each move is set up only when it plays, and the marks move again.

129
00:08:00,067 --> 00:08:02,435
有些问题要跨场景才看得出来
Some problems only show across scenes.

130
00:08:02,755 --> 00:08:07,458
在差分隐私那期，负责不同场景的智能体给同一个人起了两个名字
In the privacy video, agents building different scenes named the same person

131
00:08:07,458 --> 00:08:09,624
一部分叫 Dan，另一部分叫 Dev
Dan in one part and Dev in another.

132
00:08:09,944 --> 00:08:12,846
只有跨场景检查的评审，才能发现这种问题
Only a reviewer checking across scenes could catch that.

133
00:08:13,166 --> 00:08:17,518
另一位评审发现，隐私预算条被画成了五种不同的样子
Another reviewer found the privacy budget bar drawn five different ways.

134
00:08:17,838 --> 00:08:19,843
现在这些场景共用同一种画法
Now those scenes share one drawing.

135
00:08:22,683 --> 00:08:24,062
再说中文版
On to Chinese.

136
00:08:24,112 --> 00:08:28,555
用户要求保留那些翻成中文听着会别扭的英文术语
The user asked to keep English terms that would sound weird translated,

137
00:08:28,555 --> 00:08:30,619
并且配上中英双语字幕
with subtitles in both languages.

138
00:08:30,939 --> 00:08:34,988
关键规则是：一句英文对一句中文
The key rule: one Chinese sentence for each English sentence,

139
00:08:34,988 --> 00:08:38,704
这样每个动画触发点都还有一句话可以等
so every animation cue still has a sentence to wait for.

140
00:08:39,024 --> 00:08:41,691
有些触发点还会钉在某个具体的中文词上
Some cues are also pinned to a Chinese word.

141
00:08:43,133 --> 00:08:45,525
两种语言共用同一套场景代码
Both languages share the same scene code,

142
00:08:45,525 --> 00:08:48,850
所以智能体要检查英文版有没有被改动
so the agent checks that the English video didn't change.

143
00:08:49,170 --> 00:08:52,541
它会比对改动前后每一帧的指纹
It compares a fingerprint of every frame, before and after.

144
00:08:52,861 --> 00:08:57,277
有几个场景每次渲染的结果不完全一样，但大多数都对得上
A few scenes don't render exactly the same every time, but most match.

145
00:08:57,516 --> 00:08:58,981
那么，用哪个声音？
Then, which voice?

146
00:08:59,031 --> 00:09:02,252
智能体听不了，所以它去问语音识别模型
The agent can't listen, so it asked a speech recognizer.

147
00:09:02,572 --> 00:09:04,343
用第一个普通话声音时
With the first Mandarin voice,

148
00:09:04,343 --> 00:09:07,647
识别模型把脚本里的 noise 听成了“Nice”
the recognizer heard "Nice" where the script said noise,

149
00:09:07,647 --> 00:09:09,889
把 epsilon 听成了“Excellent”
and "Excellent" where it said epsilon.

150
00:09:10,209 --> 00:09:14,520
另一个普通话声音 17 个测试词全部通过，于是被选中了
Another Mandarin voice passed all 17 test terms, and was chosen,

151
00:09:14,520 --> 00:09:18,359
尽管有两个以英语为主的声音，分数一样高，甚至更高
though two English-first voices scored as high or higher.

152
00:09:18,679 --> 00:09:21,623
目前还没有记录显示，有人亲耳检查过它
There's no record yet of anyone checking it by ear.

153
00:09:21,866 --> 00:09:23,829
还有一条字幕，意思被弄反了
And one subtitle flipped a meaning.

154
00:09:24,149 --> 00:09:27,276
英文旁白先问 X 是不是总能赢
The English narration asks whether X always wins,

155
00:09:27,276 --> 00:09:31,679
简短地答了一句“No”，然后说电脑能做的不只是统计
answers with a short no, then says a computer can do more than count.

156
00:09:31,999 --> 00:09:36,970
中文字幕却说反了：说这不是电脑能做的事
The Chinese subtitle said the opposite: that this is not something a computer can do.

157
00:09:37,290 --> 00:09:40,213
中文版的两个 AI 评审都发现了这个问题
Both AI reviewers of the Chinese version caught it.

158
00:09:40,450 --> 00:09:41,808
这里暂停想一想
Pause on this one.

159
00:09:41,858 --> 00:09:45,250
英文那句是对的，中文说的却正好相反
The English line is right, and the Chinese says the opposite.

160
00:09:45,570 --> 00:09:47,276
这是翻译错了吗？
Was this a bad translation?

161
00:09:58,317 --> 00:10:02,339
不是。译文在那个“不是”后面本来有句号
It wasn't. The translation had a full stop after that no,

162
00:10:02,339 --> 00:10:07,341
但字幕工具把这条短字幕并进下一条时，把句号弄丢了
but the subtitle tool dropped it when it merged that short subtitle into the next.

163
00:10:07,661 --> 00:10:10,114
工具的 bug，常常看起来像内容的 bug
Tool bugs often look like content bugs.

164
00:10:10,350 --> 00:10:15,822
另一个工具 bug：拼接视频时，工具包复用了每个场景的旧片段
Another tool bug: when putting the video together, the toolkit reused each scene's old clip,

165
00:10:15,822 --> 00:10:19,630
于是改过的场景悄悄地用上了过时的画面
so edited scenes were quietly stitched from out-of-date footage.

166
00:10:19,950 --> 00:10:23,598
文件日期露了馅：片段比代码还旧
The file dates gave it away: the clips were older than the code.

167
00:10:23,918 --> 00:10:29,444
现在，只要场景比它的源文件旧，或者它的语音换了，就会重新渲染
Now a scene is rendered again whenever it's older than its sources, or its voice has changed.

168
00:10:30,734 --> 00:10:32,334
修改本身也要检查
Fixes need checking too.

169
00:10:32,633 --> 00:10:37,291
差分隐私的中文版，评审一共提了 103 条意见
For the Chinese privacy video, reviewers raised 103 points,

170
00:10:37,291 --> 00:10:41,081
大多是润色，负责修改的智能体做了 75 处改动
most of them polish, and fixers made 75 changes.

171
00:10:41,401 --> 00:10:46,137
接着，持怀疑态度的核查者检查了这些修改，又做了 12 处更正
Then skeptical verifiers checked the fixers' work, and made 12 more corrections.

172
00:10:46,457 --> 00:10:52,281
一段中文最多只能比英文长 15%，否则动画就会卡住
A Chinese passage may run at most 15 percent longer than the English, or the animation stalls.

173
00:10:52,601 --> 00:10:55,417
有个修改者说，某一段现在不超限了
One fixer said a passage now fit that limit.

174
00:10:55,737 --> 00:10:59,192
核查者实际测了时长：长了 15.3%
A verifier timed it: 15.3 percent longer.

175
00:11:02,233 --> 00:11:03,612
那下一步呢？
So what's next?

176
00:11:03,662 --> 00:11:06,649
最大的缺口，恰恰在测量够不着的地方
The biggest gaps sit exactly where measuring runs out.

177
00:11:06,969 --> 00:11:10,169
第一，也是最重要的：只有人能做的事
First, and most important: what only people can do.

178
00:11:10,489 --> 00:11:13,513
有记录的人类反馈只有用户的
The only human feedback on record is the user's:

179
00:11:13,513 --> 00:11:18,553
给长视频加背景音乐，再做一个更短、更紧凑的版本
add background music to the long videos, and make a shorter, denser version too.

180
00:11:18,873 --> 00:11:23,353
目前还没有记录显示，有人逐句亲耳检查过旁白
There's no record yet of anyone checking the narration line by line, by ear.

181
00:11:23,673 --> 00:11:26,089
有记录的试看观众全是模拟的
Every test viewer on record was simulated,

182
00:11:26,089 --> 00:11:28,964
至于大家到底学到了什么，目前也还没有衡量
and there's no measure yet of what anyone learned.

183
00:11:29,200 --> 00:11:34,208
智能体自己拍板的事，也应该由人再看一遍：差分隐私那期的长度
People should also revisit the agent's own calls: the length of the privacy video,

184
00:11:34,208 --> 00:11:40,314
中文声音的选择，保留哪些英文术语，以及对用户程序的那些小改动
the choice of Chinese voice, which English terms to keep, and the small edits to the user's program.

185
00:11:43,550 --> 00:11:45,143
第二，工程方面
Second, engineering.

186
00:11:45,193 --> 00:11:48,741
免费的中文语音没有授权用于公开发布的视频
The free Chinese voice isn't licensed for published videos,

187
00:11:48,741 --> 00:11:52,830
所以中文版发布之前，需要换成有授权的语音
so the Chinese versions need a licensed voice before they're posted.

188
00:11:53,150 --> 00:11:57,523
时间应该按词来定，而不是按字符，这样手动设的偏移就能去掉了
Timing should follow words, not characters, so the hand-set shifts can go.

189
00:11:57,843 --> 00:12:00,126
共用的部件还能让场景代码变少
And shared parts would shrink the scene code.

190
00:12:04,533 --> 00:12:09,440
第三，字幕：在中文版的评审意见里，字幕问题最多
Third, subtitles, the biggest source of review findings in the Chinese versions.

191
00:12:09,760 --> 00:12:13,194
每条字幕在哪儿断行，是由手写的规则决定的
Hand-written rules decide where each subtitle line breaks.

192
00:12:13,514 --> 00:12:17,196
第一次重写这些规则时，大部分目标都修好了
The first rewrite of those rules fixed most of its targets,

193
00:12:17,196 --> 00:12:19,317
却让另外 11 条字幕变差了
but made 11 other subtitles worse.

194
00:12:19,637 --> 00:12:24,672
又花了三轮才把它们修好，所以下次要先写测试用例
It took three more rounds to fix those, so next time, the test cases come first.

195
00:12:24,992 --> 00:12:28,661
可以让语法分析工具来建议断在哪儿，再由规则来检查
A grammar tool could suggest the breaks, and the rules could check them.

196
00:12:29,400 --> 00:12:32,835
最后一项，也最接近用户的设想：交互
Last, and closest to the user's vision: interactivity.

197
00:12:33,155 --> 00:12:36,224
前两期视频各配了一个交互页面
The first two videos each come with a playground,

198
00:12:36,224 --> 00:12:40,984
也就是一个可以自己动手试的小网页，但它和视频是分开的
a small web page to try the idea yourself, but it sits apart from the video.

199
00:12:41,304 --> 00:12:44,246
下一步，暂停视频时，应该直接在原地打开它
Next, pausing the video should open it right there,

200
00:12:44,246 --> 00:12:46,552
停在同样的状态，还能记住你的答案
in the same state, and keep your answer.

201
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:51,600
想自己试试吗？
Want to try this yourself?

202
00:12:51,856 --> 00:12:54,096
由人来选定学习者和问题
A human picks the learner and the question.

203
00:12:54,416 --> 00:12:56,336
先写脚本，而且把它写成代码
Write the script first, as code.

204
00:12:56,656 --> 00:12:58,256
让音频当时钟
Let the audio be the clock.

205
00:12:58,576 --> 00:13:02,096
用独立的评审，包括一个模拟观众
Use independent reviewers, including a simulated viewer.

206
00:13:02,416 --> 00:13:05,467
感知不到的，就去测量，修改也要再检查
Measure what you can't perceive, and check the fixes too.

207
00:13:05,787 --> 00:13:07,536
还有，每一步都存成文件
And keep every step in a file.

208
00:13:07,783 --> 00:13:09,447
最重要的是，记住目标
Above all, remember the goal.

209
00:13:09,767 --> 00:13:13,671
正如用户所说，AI 不应该只是认知卸载
As the user put it, AI should not just be cognitive offloading.

210
00:13:13,991 --> 00:13:18,194
它应该让知识更容易获得，同时还能让你学得一样深
It should make knowledge easier to reach, and still let you learn just as deeply.

211
00:13:18,433 --> 00:13:19,791
最后还有一件事
One last thing.

212
00:13:19,841 --> 00:13:23,808
这期视频也是这样做出来的，所以它有同样的盲区
This video was made the same way, so it has the same blind spot:

213
00:13:23,808 --> 00:13:26,412
做它的智能体，没法听它
the agent that made it can't listen to it.

214
00:13:26,732 --> 00:13:30,099
但你可以。如果哪里听着不对，或者让你听糊涂了
You can. If anything sounded wrong, or lost you,

215
00:13:30,099 --> 00:13:32,236
请在评论区说一声，带上时间点
say so in the comments, with the time.

216
00:13:32,556 --> 00:13:35,415
这正是这条流水线缺的反馈
That's exactly the feedback this pipeline is missing.
